@startuml 07-retrieval-flow

title On-demand retrieval - small context by construction (storage v3)

actor "AI Agent\n(new session)" as agent
participant "start-agent-session.sh" as start
database ".sdlc/sessions/\ncurrent-session.md" as brief
participant "sdlc-engine context" as engine
database "lessons.jsonl\n(ledger)" as ledger
database ".sdlc/index.sqlite" as sqlite
participant "Guide MCP\n(spdd_* tools)" as mcp

== Session start ==
agent -> start : resume work
start -> ledger : query records for active work id
start -> brief : write hot brief:\nactive Work ID + phase,\nRelated Past Work digest (<= 15 lines),\nquery menu
brief --> agent : read one small file

== During a phase (per-phase budget) ==
agent -> engine : context retrieve --work-id <ID>\n--kind decision|pitfall|pattern|analysis
engine -> ledger : filter by relevance
engine --> agent : record ids + titles (bounded)
agent -> engine : context show <record-id>
engine --> agent : full body for the few\nrecords that matter

== Optional backends ==
agent -> sqlite : ./scripts/sdlc.sh db query\n(when sqlite cache enabled)
agent -> mcp : spdd_workSubgraph / spdd_areaLessons /\nspdd_findByLabel / spdd_projectionStats
mcp --> agent : capped lists (20 default / 100 max,\ndescriptions truncated at 300 chars)
agent -> mcp : spdd_getLesson(id)
mcp --> agent : full untruncated record

note over agent
  Never bulk-read lessons.jsonl or whole
  directories. Canvas + phase artifacts are
  read directly; retrieval is for cross-work
  memory only.
end note

@enduml
